# Copy to `.env` (same folder as package.json). Never commit real keys.
#
# Supabase (Next.js app): set in `.env.local` or Vercel → Environment Variables
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — server-only; used to delete anonymous “Take a peek” users on
#     logout / tab close so `auth.users` + `profiles` rows are removed (never expose to the client).

#
# Gemini keys (recommended): use one key for local + previews, a different key for production.
# Create keys at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Used by:
#   • `npm run research-server` (static HTML on http://127.0.0.1:8787)
#   • `npm run dev` / Vercel — Next.js API routes read the same env vars server-side only:
#       POST /api/research
#       POST /api/financial-payoff
#       POST /api/financial-calendar
#       GET  /api/geocode?q=
#
# Local / preview “development” key:
GEMINI_API_KEY=paste-non-production-key-here
#
# For hosted previews (e.g. Vercel): Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   • GEMINI_API_KEY — set the Preview value to your non-prod key (branch deploys / PR previews).
#   • GEMINI_API_KEY — set the Production value to your production-only key.
# Use the same variable name; different values per environment is the usual pattern.
#
# Optional fallback alias (same semantics as GEMINI_API_KEY):
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Optional: default is gemini-2.5-flash (see https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# CORS for npm run research-server (see server/market-research.mjs): loopback browser origins
# (http://127.0.0.1:*, localhost, ::1) are allowed without this. For a static site on another
# origin (e.g. GitHub Pages) calling your API, list each full origin here or the server returns
# 403 for that browser Origin header. Comma-separated. Optional if you only use loopback.
# Example:
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourname.github.io,http://localhost:3000

# Optional: include full API key in JSON error responses (local debugging only).
# DEBUG_API_KEY_IN_ERRORS=1
